{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Aptabase’s events API, so an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to an Aptabase app’s "},{"code":"POST \/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, the app key’s header field, this encoder and its limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let aptabase = try HTTPDestination.aptabase(","    appKey: appKey,  \/\/ from the app's Instructions page: A-EU-…, A-US-… or A-SH-…","    isDebug: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose events only Debug mode should show","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON array, of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", of one event per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first. Each event is an object of these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"eventName","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sessionId","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the same way when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"props"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, flattened; left out when there are none","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"systemProps","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601, in UTC with milliseconds","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"systemProps","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds ","type":"text"},{"code":"osName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"osVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"appVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"appBuildNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s language and region (","type":"text"},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), each left out when the context has no value for it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the encoder is made with; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Aptabase requires, always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A member longer than Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its version, 50 of the app’s version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model, counted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in UTF-16) is left out and the event is sent without it, as Aptabase refuses the whole request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holding one. The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each member.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: Aptabase has no member for a user or a device. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"text":") is a session of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own: Aptabase takes no event without a session. A record a store recovers after a relaunch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its session, so it goes out in the session of its first send. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and other context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values aren’t sent. Aptabase counts users itself, from a hash of each request’s IP address and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User-Agent"},{"text":" header field with a salt it changes every day.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and so is an element of an array. Aptabase stores a string, a number or a boolean as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property’s value, and only a placeholder for an object or array, so an object or array is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spread into a property per value it holds, named after its path, joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"type":"text","text":"), and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe; one whose event name is only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace or over 60 characters; one with a property whose name, once flattened, is empty, only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace or over 40 characters, whose string value is over 180 characters, or whose number is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"too large for Aptabase; one whose values flatten to one name; one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":"; one that holds a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON can’t; one whose timestamp is outside the years 1 to 9999, or more than 23 hours before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batch is encoded; and one too large for a request ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, gives each a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked, and makes none for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for it. Aptabase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t remove duplicates, so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store’s redelivery, is counted twice. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/init(isDebug:plan:limit:now:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AptabaseEncoding"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"AptabaseBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder.swift#L74"},"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:16AptabaseEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","symbolKind":"struct","title":"AptabaseBatchEncoder"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"AptabaseEncoding"},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/AptabaseBatchEncoder/init(isDebug:plan:limit:now:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder\/init(isdebug:plan:limit:now:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDebug","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"limit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","k